.SS Versions
.PP
A version is a git tag \fBvMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH\fR\&. For each package a build uses the highest version anything requires: a package always gets at least what it asked for, and nothing newer than anyone asked for, so the same \fBktm.mod\fR always gives the same build. One major version of a package per build. A package is downloaded only when the project imports one of its directories, directly or through another package. Fetching never runs a package's code.
.PP
To publish a package: a repository whose root has a \fBktm.mod\fR and the module's \fB\&.ktm\fR files; tag a version and push the tag (\fBgit tag v0.1.0 && git push origin v0.1.0\fR). Never move a tag: \fBktm.sum\fR files that recorded it will refuse the new files.
.SS Prebuilt packages
.PP
A compiled build turns each package from the cache into a library the first time it needs it, and later builds link that library instead of compiling the package again. Nothing has to be done for it.
.IP \(bu 2
The library is made again when anything it depends on changes: the compiler, the versions the program's \fBktm.mod\fR picks, \fB\-D\fR names, \fB\-Memsafe\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
A package replaced by a directory is always compiled from source, since it is being edited; so is every package of a program whose \fBktm.mod\fR has such a replace.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-jit\fR, the REPL and builds for another \fB\-\-target\fR compile packages from source.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBKTM_PREBUILD=0\fR turns it off.
.SH Symbols
.PP
A module's names get symbols of their own (\fBgeo.area\fR is \fB_K3geo4area\fR), so they never clash with C functions or the program's names. A C function a module declares with \fBextern "c"\fR keeps its C symbol (see Calling C (see ktm-guide-calling-c(7))).
.SH Rules
.IP \(bu 2
A module is a directory; each of its files starts with \fBmodule name;\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpub\fR makes a declaration visible to importers as \fBmodule.name\fR; a method is called on a value without a prefix. Everything else is private to the module.
.IP \(bu 2
Only the defining module adds methods to a type; \fBprivate\fR hides a field outside it.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimport a, b;\fR, \fBimport a.b;\fR (used as \fBb\fR), \fBimport x = a.b;\fR, \fBimport _ = a;\fR (blank).
.IP \(bu 2
Modules are found next to the program, in the standard library, then on \fBKTM_PATH\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Import cycles, a module found twice and a global with an import's name are errors.
.IP \(bu 2
Packages are imported by path in quotes; \fBktm.mod\fR and \fBktm.sum\fR pin their versions.
